{"term":"renew","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:ce0a150d5ffd783fa5","definition":"To make (something) new again; to restore to freshness or original condition.","example":"In such a night\n Medea gather’d the enchanted herbs\n That did renew old Æson.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["autorenew","nonrenew","renewability","renewable","renew acquaintances","renewal","renewer","renewing","renewment","renew one's vows","self-renewing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/renew#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:63d29ade2300470314","definition":"To replace (something which has broken etc.); to replenish (something which has been exhausted), to keep up a required supply of.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["autorenew","nonrenew","renewability","renewable","renew acquaintances","renewal","renewer","renewing","renewment","renew one's vows","self-renewing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/renew#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3abc88f45a9721d241","definition":"To make new spiritually; to regenerate.","example":"And fassion not youre selves lyke vnto this worlde: But be ye chaunged in youre shape by the renuynge of youre wittes that ye maye fele what thynge that good yt acceptable and perfaycte will of god is.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["autorenew","nonrenew","renewability","renewable","renew acquaintances","renewal","renewer","renewing","renewment","renew one's vows","self-renewing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/renew#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:639f8de85f34aaec8c","definition":"To become new, or as new; to revive.","example":"[…] to such as are in fear they strike a great impression, renew many times, and recal such chimeras and terrible fictions into their minds.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, intransitive","wordFamily":["autorenew","nonrenew","renewability","renewable","renew acquaintances","renewal","renewer","renewing","renewment","renew one's vows","self-renewing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/renew#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:79863ead59ff1e59b4","definition":"To begin again; to recommence.","example":"This murder has been a cold case for decades until last year when the new sheriff renewed the investigation.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["autorenew","nonrenew","renewability","renewable","renew acquaintances","renewal","renewer","renewing","renewment","renew one's vows","self-renewing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/renew#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:317ae67cbf6e96c4d8","definition":"To repeat.","example":"The birds their notes renew, and bleating herds\nAttest their joy, that hill and valley rings.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"rare","register":"rare","wordFamily":["autorenew","nonrenew","renewability","renewable","renew acquaintances","renewal","renewer","renewing","renewment","renew one's vows","self-renewing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/renew#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ecc138510e5